had also been unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 24909, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GBSDhxn6WtWCtjbZDJ6dXU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 24909, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GBSDhxn6WtWCtjbZDJ6dXU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 28423, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What happened:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging before it went out.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the current state. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before anyone tries to deploy it again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Qmq4PWax4cnFr23oAMWLGM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-ap