olset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What happened:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging before it went out.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. All three regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the current state. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before anyone tries to deploy it again.", "type": "text"}]}]}